- # `↯/s.112.5` — `Sse.Error`
+ # `↯/s.112.5` — `Sse.Error`

- Raised when Obligatory cannot parse a server-sent event.
+ Levée lorsque Obligatory ne peut pas analyser un événement envoyé par le serveur.

- ## Cause
+ ## Cause

- SSE messages are framed as `field: value` lines, with `field`
- restricted to `event`, `data`, `id`, or `retry`. The `SseSource`
- class also enforces a replay-buffer capacity. When any of these
- expectations is violated, this error is raised. The constructor
- takes a `reason: Reason`; the rendered message is `the
- server-sent event was not valid because $reason`.
+ Les messages SSE sont tramés en lignes `field: value`, où `field` est restreint à `event`,
+ `data`, `id` ou `retry`. La classe `SseSource` impose aussi une capacité au tampon de rejeu.
+ Lorsque l'une de ces attentes n'est pas respectée, cette erreur est levée. Le constructeur prend
+ une `reason: Reason` ; le message affiché est `the server-sent event was not valid because $reason`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ### `↯/s.112.5.1` — `MalformedField`
+ ### `↯/s.112.5.1` — `MalformedField`

- A line in the SSE stream did not contain the required `:`
- separator between field name and value.
+ Une ligne du flux SSE ne contenait pas le séparateur `:` requis entre le nom du champ et sa
+ valeur.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.112.5.1] the server-sent event was not valid because a line did not contain the expected field: value separator`
+ **Exemple.** `[↯/s.112.5.1] the server-sent event was not valid because a line did not contain the expected field: value separator`

- **Resolution.** Verify the producer is emitting valid SSE frames;
- each non-empty line must contain a colon.
+ **Résolution.** Vérifiez que le producteur émet des trames SSE valides ; chaque ligne non vide
+ doit contenir un deux-points.

- ### `↯/s.112.5.2` — `UnknownField`
+ ### `↯/s.112.5.2` — `UnknownField`

- A field name other than `event`, `data`, `id`, or `retry` was
- encountered.
+ Un nom de champ autre que `event`, `data`, `id` ou `retry` a été rencontré.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.112.5.2] the server-sent event was not valid because the field name was not one of event, data, id, or retry`
+ **Exemple.** `[↯/s.112.5.2] the server-sent event was not valid because the field name was not one of event, data, id, or retry`

- **Resolution.** Strip non-standard fields before parsing; or extend
- the parser to accept the field.
+ **Résolution.** Retirez les champs non standard avant l'analyse, ou étendez l'analyseur pour
+ qu'il accepte le champ.

- ### `↯/s.112.5.3` — `BadRetryValue`
+ ### `↯/s.112.5.3` — `BadRetryValue`

- The `retry` field's value was not a parseable integer.
+ La valeur du champ `retry` n'était pas un entier analysable.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.112.5.3] the server-sent event was not valid because the retry field value could not be parsed as an integer`
+ **Exemple.** `[↯/s.112.5.3] the server-sent event was not valid because the retry field value could not be parsed as an integer`

- **Resolution.** The `retry` value must be a plain decimal integer
- (milliseconds).
+ **Résolution.** La valeur de `retry` doit être un simple entier décimal (en millisecondes).

- ### `↯/s.112.5.4` — `CapacityExceeded`
+ ### `↯/s.112.5.4` — `CapacityExceeded`

- The replay range requested from `SseSource.stream(start)` was
- larger than the source's circular buffer capacity, so older events
- have been overwritten.
+ L'intervalle de rejeu demandé à `SseSource.stream(start)` dépassait la capacité du tampon
+ circulaire de la source ; les événements plus anciens ont donc été écrasés.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.112.5.4] the server-sent event was not valid because the requested replay range exceeded the source buffer capacity`
+ **Exemple.** `[↯/s.112.5.4] the server-sent event was not valid because the requested replay range exceeded the source buffer capacity`

- **Resolution.** Increase the source's `capacity`, or request a more
- recent `start` index.
+ **Résolution.** Augmentez la `capacity` de la source, ou demandez un index `start` plus récent.

